  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Uganda WB Tax Justice Project Documen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2020, the Government of Uganda launched a national Domestic Revenue Mobilization (DRM) Strategy. In the two years leading up to this, Oxfam in Uganda, along with the Tax Justice Alliance Uganda (TJA-U) and other strategic partners, invested in influencing this5-year DRM strategy. As a result of this advocacy, the government&#x2019;s final tax reform agenda includes several priorities pushed by Oxfam and TJA-U alongside its CSO members. It is now critical that these reforms and commitments are implemented, and equally important how donors &#x2013; such as World Bank &#x2013; support this initiative and influence government decisions.

It is imperative to conduct a critical assessment of Uganda&#x2019;s Tax expenditure management process. This will generate policy reform proposals for the improvement of the TE management process and will inform the TE governance framework currently being developed; including the technical assistance provided by the world Bank to Uganda.

Oxfam, SEATINI (which hosts the TJA-U) and CBTP, are keen to see through the influencing work it started in 2018 &#x2013; and engage the government and World Bank on progressive tax reform priorities, including a new reform on the governance framework for tax expenditures in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
